{{!-- THE TRANSFORM: inbound schema (urn:sutra:cdr) -> storage schema (urn:sutra:call-log),
      one row at a time.

      A Handlebars SCRIPT task, not a template service task, and the difference is the point: a
      template's render becomes a reply (bytes on the wire), while a script's render must be a
      JSON OBJECT whose entries merge — typed — into the instance variables. That is what lets
      the very next node write `entry` straight into the projected store, with no second process
      and no round trip through a channel to turn bytes back into a record.

      `row` is the multi-instance item: one already-XSD-validated CallDetailRecord. Its numeric
      fields arrive as NUMBERS (the codec applied the XSD's leaf types to the CSV's untyped
      cells), so they render unquoted below and stay numeric all the way into the column.

      What the transform actually does — the two schemas are not a rename apart:
        recordId    -> entryId            renamed
        msisdn      -> subscriber         renamed
        peerMsisdn  -> counterparty       renamed
        startTime   -> startedAt          renamed
        durationSec -> durationSeconds    renamed
        cellId      -> cellSite           renamed, optional both sides
        chargeAmount-> ratedAmount        renamed
        direction   -> bearing            VOCABULARY mapped (originated/received -> outgoing/incoming)
        (derived)   -> billable           a field the inbound record does not carry
        rateCode    -> (dropped)          an inbound field storage does not keep

      Handlebars renders strict: a missing value aborts the render rather than emitting an empty
      field, so a drift between the two schemas fails loudly on the record that hit it. `eq` is
      null-tolerant, which is why it is safe inside #if. An absent cellId renders JSON null, which
      the projected store writes as a NULL column — the same thing minOccurs="0" means. --}}
{"entry":{
  "entryId":         "{{row.recordId}}",
  "subscriber":      "{{row.msisdn}}",
  "counterparty":    "{{row.peerMsisdn}}",
  "startedAt":       "{{row.startTime}}",
  "durationSeconds":  {{row.durationSec}},
  "bearing":         "{{#if (eq row.direction "originated")}}outgoing{{else}}incoming{{/if}}",
  "cellSite":        {{#if row.cellId}}"{{row.cellId}}"{{else}}null{{/if}},
  "ratedAmount":      {{row.chargeAmount}},
  "billable":         {{#if (eq row.direction "originated")}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}
}}
